WEBVTT

00:00:09,420 --> 00:00:15,180
I took a KVMO fit 22 plus got permeability test

00:00:15,180 --> 00:00:16,940
about four months ago.

00:00:16,940 --> 00:00:19,580
One thing it showed me was a sensitivity to coffee.

00:00:19,580 --> 00:00:24,580
So I switched from coffee enemas to yearma mate enemas.

00:00:24,580 --> 00:00:26,820
I would like to retest.

00:00:26,820 --> 00:00:30,340
Does it make sense to retest now?

00:00:30,340 --> 00:00:32,300
Well, I'm not doing coffee enemas

00:00:32,300 --> 00:00:36,100
and see if the coffee protein shows up at the test.

00:00:36,140 --> 00:00:40,180
Or would it be more productive to start the coffee enemas

00:00:40,180 --> 00:00:43,180
back up again and do the test after the coffee enemas

00:00:43,180 --> 00:00:46,460
again for about a month and see if the coffee proteins

00:00:46,460 --> 00:00:48,540
show up again in the test.

00:00:48,540 --> 00:00:50,700
Well, this is long been the discussion

00:00:50,700 --> 00:00:53,020
of functional practitioners.

00:00:53,020 --> 00:00:56,740
Whether you should, okay, let's say same example would be

00:00:56,740 --> 00:00:59,220
I think a sensitive to gluten.

00:00:59,220 --> 00:01:01,740
So I went gluten free.

00:01:01,740 --> 00:01:03,940
I've been gluten free for three months.

00:01:03,940 --> 00:01:06,820
And then I did a blood test to find out

00:01:06,820 --> 00:01:08,580
if I have gluten sensitivity.

00:01:08,580 --> 00:01:11,660
Was that why is there should I go back on gluten

00:01:11,660 --> 00:01:16,660
to see if I have more gluten peptide circulated in my body?

00:01:18,020 --> 00:01:20,340
Am I going to pick up a greater sensitivity?

00:01:23,340 --> 00:01:25,660
The way I've always answered that is,

00:01:25,660 --> 00:01:28,660
okay, how are you living your life?

00:01:28,660 --> 00:01:33,660
Are you not eating that food on a regular basis anyhow?

00:01:34,940 --> 00:01:38,620
And you plan to stay gluten free?

00:01:38,620 --> 00:01:40,180
Yes, I plan to stay gluten free.

00:01:40,180 --> 00:01:41,540
How I feel better gluten free.

00:01:41,540 --> 00:01:45,260
Okay, well then do the test again be gluten free.

00:01:45,260 --> 00:01:47,100
Or no, I want to go back on gluten.

00:01:47,100 --> 00:01:50,180
Well, then it might be good to eat a little gluten

00:01:50,180 --> 00:01:52,580
and because I haven't felt any different

00:01:52,580 --> 00:01:54,340
being off of gluten will eat some gluten

00:01:54,340 --> 00:01:55,380
and then do the test again.

00:01:55,380 --> 00:01:58,860
If it comes back positive, gluten isn't a good example

00:01:58,860 --> 00:02:02,540
because if you have, if you show gliated peptides,

00:02:03,380 --> 00:02:07,060
you're probably never going to be able to go back on gluten.

00:02:07,060 --> 00:02:10,140
So that's not wasn't a good example in my question,

00:02:10,140 --> 00:02:13,940
but in this case, I would say it might be better

00:02:13,940 --> 00:02:17,700
to go back on the coffee enemas, do that for a month

00:02:17,700 --> 00:02:21,340
and then retest to see if it comes back positive

00:02:21,340 --> 00:02:24,300
because you do want to be on the coffee enemas.

00:02:24,300 --> 00:02:27,580
So I think that would be a better test.

00:02:27,580 --> 00:02:29,980
So the question is really,

00:02:29,980 --> 00:02:33,420
should I put my body under that environmental stress

00:02:33,420 --> 00:02:34,900
when I do the test?

00:02:34,900 --> 00:02:38,100
Or should I try to stay off of it and do the test?

00:02:39,140 --> 00:02:43,300
The argument is if you stay off of it and do the test,

00:02:43,300 --> 00:02:46,340
it might show negative now so you think you're okay

00:02:46,340 --> 00:02:48,580
and then as soon as you go back on it again,

00:02:48,580 --> 00:02:50,500
your body flares up in immune response

00:02:50,500 --> 00:02:53,540
and you start making IGG and IGA antibodies

00:02:53,540 --> 00:02:56,420
against that thing with this case coffee

00:02:56,420 --> 00:02:58,060
and you're back in the square and what again

00:02:58,220 --> 00:03:00,940
you're causing inflammation.

00:03:00,940 --> 00:03:04,980
So I think it's better to put your body under stress

00:03:04,980 --> 00:03:08,860
in a case like this, whatever you want to go back to

00:03:08,860 --> 00:03:11,180
then put it back under that stress

00:03:11,180 --> 00:03:12,860
and see if it comes up positive.

00:03:14,780 --> 00:03:15,860
I didn't even finish the question.

00:03:15,860 --> 00:03:19,140
I'm asking a relation to my breast lump

00:03:19,140 --> 00:03:21,380
which is very close to the surface.

00:03:21,380 --> 00:03:25,020
While a while ago I asked if it would be smart

00:03:25,020 --> 00:03:27,780
to do a contrast therapy heat or cold over the lump

00:03:27,780 --> 00:03:31,180
to stress it and you said yes to try that.

00:03:31,180 --> 00:03:34,100
I got to think and know that the contrast therapy

00:03:34,100 --> 00:03:36,820
also increases blood flow to the area

00:03:36,820 --> 00:03:39,100
and I thought that was something that we're trying

00:03:39,100 --> 00:03:42,740
not to do with tumor so can you explain

00:03:42,740 --> 00:03:45,220
the seemingly conflict of this?

00:03:45,220 --> 00:03:47,460
Well, if you're finished with cold,

00:03:47,460 --> 00:03:49,540
I should have been more specific

00:03:49,540 --> 00:03:52,540
than you're not necessarily increasing blood flow.

00:03:52,540 --> 00:03:54,820
For instance, it's very common with somebody

00:03:54,820 --> 00:03:56,580
with muscular skeletal injury,

00:03:56,580 --> 00:03:58,140
let's say you sprayed your ankle.

00:03:58,140 --> 00:04:00,140
They say, what do they say?

00:04:00,140 --> 00:04:07,140
You know, rest, which is to elevate and to put cool on it

00:04:07,140 --> 00:04:11,420
and to put always iced it and things like that.

00:04:11,420 --> 00:04:12,900
What's the acronym it's called?

00:04:12,900 --> 00:04:17,900
Rice, it's rest, ice, I don't forget.

00:04:20,380 --> 00:04:24,620
But to help with the sprayed ankle.

00:04:24,620 --> 00:04:27,780
But the truth is, you know, if you've worked with people

00:04:27,780 --> 00:04:32,140
with muscular skeletal injuries like I have years ago,

00:04:32,140 --> 00:04:35,620
many times people react negatively to cold

00:04:35,620 --> 00:04:40,100
and they work more positively to heat or vice versa.

00:04:40,100 --> 00:04:41,540
Everybody's different.

00:04:41,540 --> 00:04:44,380
So what are the ways that you can help with that

00:04:44,380 --> 00:04:46,300
is to alternate hot and cold.

00:04:46,300 --> 00:04:48,980
Just like do a minute of cold, a minute of heat,

00:04:48,980 --> 00:04:52,180
a minute of cold, a minute of heat

00:04:52,180 --> 00:04:54,300
and then finish with cold.

00:04:54,300 --> 00:05:00,980
And see if that pumping action actually helps with the healing.

00:05:00,980 --> 00:05:06,940
So that can be something to try.

00:05:06,940 --> 00:05:10,860
And with doing anything like over a tumor or something,

00:05:10,860 --> 00:05:16,020
you want to be very careful and be extra-visual to see

00:05:16,020 --> 00:05:21,060
if you felt like that did not feel good.

00:05:21,060 --> 00:05:22,780
I would say make it worse right away.

00:05:23,620 --> 00:05:27,940
It wasn't helping and then you would scratch that.

00:05:27,940 --> 00:05:29,820
But everybody's a little bit different.

00:05:29,820 --> 00:05:33,500
And it's worth a try to see if something helps.

